      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 American College of Foot and Ankle Surgeons. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Freiberg disease is a chronic progressive condition that results in pain and loss of normal function of the metatarsophalangeal joint (MTPJ). We describe a case of acute Freiberg disease secondary to a short course of oral steroids. The patient presented with an acute metatarsal head fracture that was managed successfully with open reduction and internal fixation. Although a rare complication of corticosteroid use, physicians having patients start taking steroids must remember the risk of osteonecrosis."
      },
